41	
42	Static parameters may include one or more
43	\KWD{nat} and \KWD{int} parameters.
44	Syntactically, a \KWD{nat} parameter consists of
45	\KWD{nat} followed by an identifier.
46	An \KWD{int} parameter consists of
47	\KWD{int} followed by an identifier.
48	These parameters are instantiated at runtime with numeric values.
49	A \KWD{nat} parameter may be used to instantiate other
50	\KWD{nat} parameters, or to appear in any context that a
51	variable of type \EXP{\mathbb{N}32} can appear,
52	except that it cannot be assigned to.
53	An \KWD{int} parameter may be used to instantiate other
54	\KWD{int} parameters, or to appear in any context that a
55	variable of type \EXP{\mathbb{Z}32} can appear,
56	except that it cannot be assigned to.
